{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy this to .cursor/mcp.json and paste your own Supabase personal access token.",
    "The real file is gitignored because the token grants access to every project on the account.",
    "Create a token at https://supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens",
    "",
    "--project-ref pins the server to the Ron & Friends database (opxyeajywipsitwecgcz)",
    "so it cannot reach the other leagues on the same account — in particular not",
    "ultimate-keeper-league (xqhkhcmphvytoibjewqi), which this tree was copied from and",
    "which holds a real completed draft. If you see that ref here or in .cursor/mcp.json,",
    "it is the stale one and every schema you inspect will be the wrong league's.",
    "",
    "The pin does NOT isolate this app's tables, because it cannot: the R&F project also",
    "hosts the deployed app at ron-and-friends-fantasy.vercel.app in its `public` schema,",
    "and the two schemas collide on fourteen table names. This app is in `redraft` (see",
    "src/lib/db-schema.mjs), so read results carefully — `teams` means two different",
    "tables here. --read-only is what makes that safe rather than merely confusing.",
    "",
    "--read-only also keeps schema changes in supabase/redraft-schema.sql, where they",
    "belong. Note that this repo does NOT push migrations: the project's migration",
    "ledger belongs to ../RonAndFriendsApp. See that file's header.",
    "",
    "fantasypros needs no token here. It is OAuth-protected (scope user:read) against",
    "secure.fantasypros.com, so Cursor prompts for a browser sign-in the first time a",
    "tool is called. This entry is for exploring the server from the editor.",
    "",
    "THIS IS NOT THE GRANT THE APP USES. Cursor's sign-in lives in the editor and a",
    "deployment has no browser to renew it with, so the app holds its own grant:",
    "npm run auth:fantasypros, stored in fantasypros_oauth and refreshed server-side.",
    "See docs/FANTASYPROS-MCP.md. The draft board still reads only the committed",
    "snapshot in data/, which is what makes an outage a non-event."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "supabase": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "-y",
        "@supabase/mcp-server-supabase@latest",
        "--read-only",
        "--project-ref=opxyeajywipsitwecgcz"
      ],
      "env": {
        "SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN": "sbp_your_token_here"
      }
    },
    "fantasypros": {
      "url": "https://api.fantasypros.com/mcp"
    }
  }
}
